{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/prf-unital-groebner-decomposition","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:unital-groebner-decomposition","kind":"proof","uses":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/thm-unital-groebner-decomposition","papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/lem-generator-choice","papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-division-algorithm"],"text":"main-theorem-proof.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prf:unital-groebner-decomposition\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f \\in A</code>. The <a href=\"#def:division-algorithm\">division algorithm</a>\nwrites <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f = r + \\tilde{f}</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r \\in O(I)</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tilde{f} \\in I</code>.\nBy <a href=\"#lem:generator-choice\">Lemma (generator choice)</a>, we can take\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r \\in \\tilde{O}(G)</code>. As <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f</code> is arbitrary, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A = I + \\tilde{O}(G)</code>.</p>\n<p>It remains to show the sum is direct, which follows from uniqueness\nof <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r</code>. Suppose the division algorithm produces two representations:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  f = \\tilde{f} + r = \\tilde{f}' + r'.</code></pre>\n<p>Then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tilde{f} - \\tilde{f}' \\in I</code>, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r - r' \\in I</code>. If\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r - r' \\neq 0</code>, then by\n<a href=\"#lem:generator-choice\">Lemma (generator choice)</a> there exists\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g_\\gamma \\in G</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{LT}(g_\\gamma) \\mid (r - r')</code>.\nBut by construction of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r'</code>, no such <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g_\\gamma</code> exists —\ncontradiction. Thus <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r = r'</code> and the sum is direct.</p>\n","source":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/main-theorem-proof.md","heading":"Proof"}
